# 🧠 What is CI/CD?

## Continuous Integration (CI)

Continuous Integration means automatically testing and validating code whenever new changes are pushed to a shared repository.

In this project:

```text
Code Push
    ↓
Install Dependencies
    ↓
Run Unit Tests
    ↓
Build Application
```

If the tests fail, the workflow stops.

```text
Code
 ↓
Unit Tests
 ↓
❌ Failed
 ↓
Pipeline Stops
```

This prevents broken code from moving further in the pipeline.

---

## Continuous Delivery / Deployment (CD)

After the code passes the CI stage, it can be packaged and prepared for deployment.

In this project:

```text
Tests Passed
     ↓
Docker Build
     ↓
Docker Image
     ↓
Docker Hub
     ↓
Deployment
```

Docker Hub acts as a **container registry** where the Docker image is stored.

